  "rationales": {"U":"'The product must be available on both Windows and Linux operating platforms' lacks platform version specificity (e.g., Windows 10+ or Ubuntu 20.04 LTS), and 'The execution of the application must be kept on the server side' is vague about what 'execution' means (code loading? UI rendering? API invocation?). Also, 'timely manner – see time restrictions' refers to undefined external content, breaking self-containment.", "A":"'Available on both Windows and Linux' is ambiguous: does it mean binary compatibility, containerized deployment, or source compilation? 'Kept on the server side' conflicts with typical client-server interpretations — e.g., is JavaScript execution forbidden? No definition of 'server side' scope is provided.", "C":"No factual inconsistency is evident; cross-platform support and server-side execution are technically feasible and internally consistent. However, 'timely manner' is underspecified but not factually incorrect — hence score 3.", "V":"None of the three clauses are testable as written: no measurable criteria for 'available', no observable indicator for 'kept on the server side', and 'timely manner' has no defined deadline, success metric, or measurement method — violating verifiability at a foundational level."},
  "suggestions": {"U":"Replace entire requirement with three atomic, self-contained statements specifying OS versions, deployment artifacts, and timing constraints.","A":"The product shall run natively as a 64-bit executable on Windows 10 or later and Ubuntu 22.04 LTS or later; all application logic and data processing shall execute exclusively on the configured application server; the system shall deliver a response to any user-initiated request within ≤2 seconds under 95th-percentile load.","C":"Keep unchanged, but clarify 'timely manner' by anchoring to a concrete schedule milestone or SLA — e.g., 'shall be delivered no later than 2025-06-30' or 'shall meet all deadlines in Project Schedule v2.1'.","V":"The product shall install and launch without error on Windows 10 (Build 19045+) and Ubuntu 22.04 LTS (kernel 5.15+) using the provided .msi and .deb packages; network traffic analysis shall confirm zero client-side JavaScript execution of business logic; end-to-end request-response latency shall be ≤2 s for 95% of requests at 100 concurrent users, measured via JMeter script 'LoadTest_R1.jmx'."},
